@startuml

title Compute job lifecycle: batch, workunit, and result states

hide empty description

state "=batch=" as batch {
    state "open" as b_open
    state "dispatched" as b_disp
    state "closed" as b_closed
}

state "=workunit=" as wu {
    state "no canonical result" as w_pend
    state "canonical result set" as w_done
}

state "=result=" as res {
    state "1 Inactive" as r_inact
    state "2 Unsent" as r_unsent
    state "4 InProgress" as r_prog
    state "5 Done\n(outcome 1 Success /\n3 ClientError / 4 NoReply)" as r_done
}

b_open --> b_disp : dispatch-batch saved every\nworkunit of the batch
b_disp --> b_closed : assimilator: every workunit\nhas a canonical result

w_pend --> w_done : validator accepts a Done result\n(done count reaches target_redundancy)

r_unsent --> r_done : submit (JetStream path;\nhost bound and outcome\nrecorded at submit time)
r_unsent --> r_prog : legacy pull channel:\nhost claims the result
r_prog --> r_done : submit (pull path)
r_prog --> r_unsent : reaper: host heartbeats\nstale for over 5 minutes

note right of r_unsent
    created by the workunit dispatcher
    when the assignment is published;
    stays Unsent while the node runs
end note
note right of r_inact
    reserved; no current flow
    writes this state
end note
note right of w_done
    the workunit has no status column;
    canonical_result_id is the marker
end note
note right of b_closed
    batch_workflow_bridge fires
    step_completed_event for batches
    linked to a workflow step
end note

@enduml
